.Dd October 20, 2026
.Dt APROCFS 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm aprocfs
.Nd process file system in the layout of Android
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To load the file system as a module at boot time, place the following
line in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
aprocfs_load="YES"
.Ed
.Pp
To mount it in a jail, add a line such as the following to
.Xr jail.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mount += "aprocfs $path/proc aprocfs rw 0 0";
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
file system gives a
.Pa /proc
tree with the names and the text layout that Android programs read
on Linux.
It is intended for a jail that runs Android programs on the native
.Fx
ABI.
The values are
.Fx
values: signal numbers, scheduling policies, thread identifiers and the
.Xr uname 3
strings are those of
.Fx .
.Pp
.Nm
does not use the
.Xr linux 4
ABI and does not change
.Xr procfs 4 .
A program sees
.Nm
only where it is mounted.
.Pp
The top level directory contains:
.Bl -tag -width "sys/kernel/pid_max"
.It Pa self
A symbolic link to the directory of the reading process.
.It Pa version
One line:
the
.Va kern.ostype
value, the word
.Dq version ,
the
.Va kern.osrelease
value and the
.Va kern.version
value in parentheses.
The values are those that the reader sees, so a jail with its own
.Va osrelease
shows that value.
.It Pa sys/kernel/pid_max
One more than the largest process or thread identifier:
.Dv NO_PID
plus the
.Va kern.maxthread
value.
.It Pa <pid>
A directory for each process that the reader can see.
A thread identifier also names a directory, which is not listed.
It shows the same files as
.Pa <pid>/task/<tid> .
.El
.Pp
Each process directory contains:
.Bl -tag -width "status"
.It Pa cmdline
The arguments of the process, each followed by a NUL byte, as the
.Va kern.proc.args
sysctl gives them.
It is empty for a zombie and for a system process.
.It Pa comm
The name of the first thread, or the command name if the thread has
no name, and a newline.
The name has at most 15 bytes.
.It Pa exe
A symbolic link to the executable, as the
.Va kern.proc.pathname
sysctl gives it.
.It Pa fd
A directory with one entry for each open file descriptor.
See
.Sx File descriptors .
.It Pa maps
One line for each entry of the address space, as the
.Va kern.proc.vmmap
sysctl gives them:
the start and end addresses, the protection, the letter
.Ql s
for a shared entry or
.Ql p
for a private one, the offset, the device, the inode number and the
path.
The path column shows
.Ql [stack]
for the stack and
.Ql [vdso]
for the shared page.
.It Pa stat
One line of 52 fields, in the order of the Linux
.Pa stat
file.
Times are in ticks of 100 Hz.
The priority field is 20 plus the nice value for a timeshare thread,
and the negative real-time priority minus one for a real-time thread.
Fields that
.Fx
has no source for are 0.
The address fields are 0 unless the reader can debug the process.
.It Pa status
One field on each line, the name and a tab, then the value.
Signal sets have 128 bits and show as 32 hexadecimal digits;
bit
.Ar n Ns \-1
is signal
.Ar n .
The capability sets are 0.
.It Pa task
A directory with one subdirectory for each thread, named by its thread
identifier.
A thread directory has
.Pa cmdline ,
.Pa comm ,
.Pa exe ,
.Pa fd ,
.Pa maps ,
.Pa stat
and
.Pa status ,
with the values of that thread where a thread has its own value.
.El
.Ss File descriptors
Each entry of
.Pa fd
is named by the descriptor number.
.Xr readlink 2
of an entry gives the path of the file when the kernel knows it.
Such an entry is a symbolic link:
.Xr open 2 ,
.Xr stat 2
and
.Xr realpath 3
follow the path.
.Pp
For any other descriptor,
.Xr readlink 2
gives a description:
.Ql pipe:[inode] ,
.Ql socket:[inode] ,
.Ql anon_inode:[kqueue] ,
.Ql anon_inode:[eventfd] ,
.Ql anon_inode:[timerfd] ,
.Ql anon_inode:inotify ,
.Ql anon_inode:[pidfd] ,
the path of a named shared memory object,
.Ql /memfd:\ (deleted)
for an anonymous one, or
.Ql /#inode
for a file whose path is not known, followed by
.Ql \ (deleted)
when the file has no links.
Such an entry is not a symbolic link.
Opening an entry of the calling process duplicates the descriptor, as
.Xr fdescfs 4
does.
Opening an entry of another process fails.
.Pp
For an
.Dv O_TMPFILE
file that has never had a name, the description is
.Ql <directory>/#<inode> (deleted) .
The directory path is saved at creation and is relative to the reader's
jail root, as in
.Dv F_KINFO
of
.Xr fcntl 2 .
It does not follow directory renames or removals.
If the path was unavailable at creation or is outside the reader's jail,
the description remains
.Ql /#<inode> (deleted) .
The entry still duplicates the descriptor when opened.
A successful
.Xr linkat 2
discards the saved path.
.Ss Access
A process directory is visible only to readers that
.Xr p_cansee 9
allows, which includes the jail check.
.Pa fd
and
.Pa maps
also need the permission of
.Xr p_candebug 9 ,
as the
.Va kern.proc.filedesc
and
.Va kern.proc.vmmap
sysctls do.
All files are read-only.
.Xr fsync 2
and
.Xr fdatasync 2
on any node fail with
.Er EINVAL .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/proc/self/status" -compact
.It Pa /proc/version
.It Pa /proc/sys/kernel/pid_max
.It Pa /proc/self
.It Pa /proc/<pid>/stat
.It Pa /proc/<pid>/status
.It Pa /proc/<pid>/maps
.It Pa /proc/<pid>/fd/<n>
.It Pa /proc/<pid>/task/<tid>
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
To mount an
.Nm
file system on
.Pa /compat/android/proc :
.Pp
.Dl "mount -t aprocfs aprocfs /compat/android/proc"
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr procstat 1 ,
.Xr jail 2 ,
.Xr mount 2 ,
.Xr asysfs 4 ,
.Xr fdescfs 4 ,
.Xr procfs 4 ,
.Xr jail.conf 5 ,
.Xr jail 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr p_candebug 9 ,
.Xr p_cansee 9 ,
.Xr pseudofs 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
file system first appeared in the freebsd-android-native fork of
.Fx 15.1 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Ayeed Shaikh Aq Mt Ayeed.AI10@race.reva.edu.in
.Sh CAVEATS
.Nm
is not a
.Xr pseudofs 9
file system.
Its directories of threads and of file descriptors change at run time,
which
.Xr pseudofs 9
does not support.
.Sh BUGS
The open mode of a descriptor does not show in the mode of its
.Pa fd
entry.
.Pp
The
.Pa maps
path of a file in a
.Xr nullfs 4
mount is the path of the lower file.
A shared anonymous mapping shows as private.
.Pp
The priority field of
.Pa stat
does not show a priority that a timeshare thread borrows through a
priority-inheritance mutex.
